issue_context.body:
While working on #91295 I noticed that there is a special handling for `StringContent`:

https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/blob/6d3be9e69dc385722851b0c165255cc4828aec7c/src/libraries/System.Net.Http/src/System/Net/Http/BrowserHttpHandler/BrowserHttpHandler.cs#L214-L227

But because `StringContent` inherits from `ByteArrayContent` the string is actually stored as a byte array, which means that `ReadAsStringAsync` actually allocates a new string an thus needs more memory then a call to `ReadAsByteArrayAsync` would need and is also slower.
Since the browser supports sending byte array anyway I would propose to remove this special case. E.g. like this: https://github.com/campersau/runtime/commit/c887f0caf6b0329ef10272f1b8b0d4f41c7c5ec8


Currently:
string > StringContent > new byte array (encoding)
byte array > ReadAsStringAsync > new string (encoding)
string > Fetch > "complex" string to js Marshal (encoding?)

Proposed:
string > StringContent > new byte array (encoding)
byte array > ReadAsByteArrayAsync > new byte array
byte array > Fetch > easy byte array to js

Or was there any other reason why this was special cased in the first place?
Edit: Looks like it was there from the beginning: https://github.com/mono/mono/pull/10464

|               Method |     Mean |    Error |   StdDev |   Gen0 | Allocated |
|--------------------- |---------:|---------:|---------:|-------:|----------:|
|    ReadAsStringAsync | 570.8 ns | 11.39 ns | 13.99 ns | 0.0973 |    1280 B |
| ReadAsByteArrayAsync | 187.0 ns |  3.73 ns |  6.43 ns | 0.0525 |     688 B |

<details>
<summary>Benchmark</summary>

```c#
[MemoryDiagnoser]
public class Program
{
    public static void Main(string[] args)
    {
        BenchmarkRunner.Run<Program>(args: args);
    }

    private StringContent content;

    [GlobalSetup]
    public void Setup()
    {
        content = new StringContent("Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet, consetetur sadipscing elitr, sed diam nonumy eirmod tempor invidunt ut labore et dolore magna aliquyam erat, sed diam voluptua. At vero eos et accusam et justo duo dolores et ea rebum. Stet clita kasd gubergren, no sea takimata sanctus est Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet. Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet, consetetur sadipscing elitr, sed diam nonumy eirmod tempor invidunt ut labore et dolore magna aliquyam erat, sed diam voluptua. At vero eos et accusam et justo duo dolores et ea rebum. Stet clita kasd gubergren, no sea takimata sanctus est Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet.");
    }

    [Benchmark]
    public async Task ReadAsStringAsync()
    {
        await content.ReadAsStringAsync();
    }

    [Benchmark]
    public async Task ReadAsByteArrayAsync()
    {
        await content.ReadAsByteArrayAsync();
    }

}
```

</details>

---

If we really want to remove allocations I would propose adding an `internal virtual bool TryGetMemory(out ReadOnlyMemory<byte> memory);` method to `HttpContent` and implement it for `ByteArrayContent` / `StringContent` / `EmptyContent` / `FormUrlEncodedContent` / `ReadOnlyMemoryContent` and special case this instead.
